      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Our experience with 100 colonoscopic examinations are described. The clinical value of the procedure is outlined and the minimal degree of attendant morbidity, when performed by a competent endoscopist, are emphasized. The indications and contraindications for this relatively recently devised diagnostic and therapeutic modality should be commonly known. The procedure should be done whenever indicated."},
